<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franz Georg von Metternich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1746">1746</a>–<a href="/years/1818">1818</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Franz Georg von Metternich was a Rhenish count and diplomat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> service, the father of the Austrian chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klemens-von-metternich">Klemens von Metternich</a>. He served as Austrian minister in the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> until the French conquest. Having lost his family lands on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, he received the secularised abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ochsenhausen">Ochsenhausen</a> in 1803 as compensation and was raised to the rank of prince.</p></div>
